    <villain:personalityTrait>Persistence</villain:personalityTrait>
    <villain:personalityDetails>Obsession: Driven by a pathological need to surpass Alfred Borden, leading him to sacrifice his morality, wealth, and ultimately his very existence to achieve the ultimate illusion. |  | Narcissism: The Hunger for Applause — Prioritizing the audience's adoration and the "look on their faces" over the craft itself, reflecting a personality that seeks validation through external spectacle. | Persistence: The Widow’s Grief Twisted — Initially motivated by the tragic loss of his wife, his grief eventually mutates into a bitter, lifelong vendetta that blinds him to the human cost of his actions.</villain:personalityDetails>
    <schema1:description>Obsession: Driven by a pathological need to surpass Alfred Borden, leading him to sacrifice his morality, wealth, and ultimately his very existence to achieve the ultimate illusion. |  | Narcissism: The Hunger for Applause — Prioritizing the audience's adoration and the "look on their faces" over the craft itself, reflecting a personality that seeks validation through external spectacle. | Persistence: The Widow’s Grief Twisted — Initially motivated by the tragic loss of his wife, his grief eventually mutates into a bitter, lifelong vendetta that blinds him to the human cost of his actions.</schema1:description>
